    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="1645" n="1487" xml:id="pg1487"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Delegate White to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Algeciras</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. White states that, referring to his two dispatches two and seven, he would
                    be glad to hear the department’s views on the Jewish question, which he hopes to
                    bring before the conference, probably next Saturday or Monday. Mr. White also
                    states that he fears the form suggested by grand rabbi and others will be
                    inadequate and unsatisfactory to our Jewish fellow-citizens, and yet it would
                    not be wise to say anything likely to be prejudicial to Jews in Morocco.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
